# The script the default set's fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which sets nothing of a child's environment. What
# it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file and starts no
# child.
#
# The default set registers the login-shell package's base and chooses it,
# and the mise package's directory source: `layers` says, in the window mode,
# the base login-shell, looked up in the home directory `/u` with the shell
# its probes find, else /bin/zsh (`LoginShell.program`), and the one
# directory source, named mise, at the first of mise's usual places under
# `/u` (`Mise.candidates`), skipped with none; in the headless mode, the
# base inherited (login-shell is chosen, but looks nothing up there) and no
# directory source. A set that drops mise, from its lakefile's requires or
# its entry modules, says `none` for the directory sources in both modes; one
# that drops login-shell says `base inherited` in both.
reload
settle
run layers
scene
